cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SLAPBench, please cite the preprint below."
title: "SLAPBench: Benchmarking Multimodal Large Language Models for Four-Finger SLAP Fingerprint Verification"
abstract: >-
  SLAPBench is the first benchmark evaluating multimodal large language models
  on four-finger SLAP fingerprint verification, built on NIST Special Database
  302b. It evaluates 7,832 exhaustive pairs (176 genuine, 7,656 impostor)
  across four open-source models and one API model under three prompting
  regimes, and shows that task-description prompting collapses open-source
  models to near-total false acceptance while similarity-scoring prompts
  eliminate the collapse.
authors:
  - family-names: Pyakurel
    given-names: Bibesh
  - family-names: Murshed
    given-names: M. G. S.
repository-code: "https://github.com/bibeshpyakurel/SLAPBench"
url: "https://github.com/bibeshpyakurel/SLAPBench"
type: software
license: MIT
# `doi:` at this level identifies the archived *software*. Add the Zenodo DOI
# here after the first Zenodo-backed release; see docs/ZENODO.md. The preprint's
# DOI belongs to `preferred-citation` below, not here.
keywords:
  - biometrics
  - fingerprint-verification
  - multimodal-large-language-models
  - benchmark
  - NIST-SD302b
